{
  "name": "How to Prep Your Walls for a Perfect Tile Installation",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Getting your walls ready for tile isn't just about making them look clean; it's about creating a stable, long-lasting foundation. Skipping this step can lead to future headaches like cracked grout or loose tiles. First, ensure your wall surface is completely clean, dry, and free from any grease, dust, or old adhesive. Next, you'll want to check for levelness and flatness. Any bumps or dips will show through your new tile, so patching and leveling compounds are your friends here. HH Remodeling LLC always stresses the importance of a sound substrate because it truly makes all the difference in the final appearance and durability. Don't rush this part; it's the backbone of a great tile job. If your walls are particularly uneven or damaged, it might be time to bring in a professional for an assessment. They can help you determine the best course of action to ensure your tile has the perfect canvas.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
